    "canonical_name": "http.request",
    "display_name": "Make an HTTP request",
    "model_description": "Call an HTTP or HTTPS API, including localhost and LAN. method defaults to GET; headers and body are optional. GET and HEAD cannot carry a body. body accepts text or JSON (up to 1 MiB). credential selects the api_key slot or an unambiguous configured name; Core only sends it to a user-approved origin. Read-only mode requires network approval. Other modes allow ordinary network tools. GET/HEAD follow up to three redirects and remove credentials across origins. Mutating methods never automatically retry or redirect; an interrupted write may need verification. HTTP 4xx/5xx are normal results. Responses are bounded; use http.download for large or binary files. Approval does not grant file access.",
